    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.ai\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nIf I perform `va*` on `*foo*`, I expect `*foo*` is selected.\r\nHowever, the selection is `foo*`, which is missing `*` on the left.\r\n\r\nThe similar thing happens on `/` or some other symbols.\r\n\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.8 to 0.10 (unreleased)\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- setup\r\n\r\n```\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(\"/path/to/mini.nvim\")\r\nrequire(\"mini.ai\").setup({})\r\n```\r\n\r\n- do `va*` on a line: `*foo*`\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nselection is `*foo*`\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nselection is `foo*` (missing left `*`)",
